course: dictionary
lesson: 15678
title: Tidiness: neat and in order
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tidiness is a noun. It names the quality of being neat and in order, with things in their right places. You can use it for a room, a desk, a bag, or a piece of work.
explain: «Her tidiness made the classroom a calm place to work.» The word tidiness tells us the room was neat. Look at the clues around it: calm and work. A neat room helps people concentrate, so tidiness must mean neatness and order.
explain: Tidiness can also be a habit, something you do again and again. «Ben's tidiness meant he always put his toys away before bed.» Here tidiness is not one clean room, but a way of keeping things neat every day.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «Ben's neatness meant he always put his toys away». It still makes sense, so neatness is a good meaning for tidiness.
fact: Tidiness means being neat and in order, with things in their right places.
fact: Tidiness is also the habit of keeping things neat.
fact: «Tidiness» is a noun. It is uncountable, so we say «the tidiness» or «her tidiness», not «a tidiness».
fact: «Tidy» is the adjective, as in «a tidy desk». The noun for that quality is tidiness.
fact: Phrases to remember: «the tidiness of her work» and «a love of tidiness».
exercise: «The tidiness of her desk showed she was careful.» What does tidiness mean here? | Being loud and busy | Being very hungry | *Being neat and in order, with things in their right places | Being wet and grey
exercise: Mia says tidiness only means cleaning the floor once. What is the better answer? | Tidiness means a very old castle | *Tidiness is also a habit of keeping things neat, not just one clean moment | Tidiness means a loud noise in the hall | Tidiness means being late for school
exercise: Find and copy the noun in this sentence: «Teachers gave marks for the tidiness of the work.» | marks | teachers | work | *tidiness
test: «Dad admired the tidiness of his garden.» Which word is the noun for being neat? | Dad | garden | *tidiness | admired
test: Which phrase shows tidiness as a habit or a love of neatness? | a very old castle | *a love of tidiness | a loud noise in the hall | a wet grey day
exam: Which is the best meaning of tidiness? | Being loud and busy | Being very old | *Being neat and in order | Being wet and grey
